{\b\fs22 Orchicon - license and installation information}\par
\par

{\b\fs19 What this installer installed}\par
orchicon.exe   the control plane, the CLI and the orchestrator\par
orch.exe       the terminal client (TUI)\par
orchicon-desktop.exe   the desktop app (this window's sibling)\par
\par
They are per-user: nothing was written outside your own profile, and no\par
administrator rights were needed.\par
\par

{\b\fs19 What setup does next}\par
Finishing this wizard opens a console that runs {\f1 orchicon install}. It\par
downloads the host services Orchicon runs on (Postgres, NATS, the telemetry\par
plane), then starts this instance's control plane. It is idempotent: if it\par
stops, run it again and it resumes where it left off.\par
\par
Your data - databases, traces, logs and this instance's configuration - lives\par
in your own profile, under {\f1 AppData\\Local} on this machine. Uninstalling\par
Orchicon (Settings > Apps) removes the programs and leaves that data alone.\par
\par
{\b\fs19 Requirements}\par
The desktop app draws its window with Microsoft Edge WebView2, which is\par
preinstalled on Windows 11 and provisioned by the installer on Windows 10.\par
